{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "52", "S": "02"}}, "news": [{"title": "Enforcement directorate searches Prayag Developers premises in Nagpur; seizes \u20b91.95 crore cash", "para": "Recently, the Enforcement Directorate raided two sites in Nagpur that are tied to Prayag Developers & Builders. During these searches, they uncovered a whopping \u20b91.95 crore in cash. Moreover, they froze over \u20b940 lakh in bank accounts and discovered some properties that they believe are linked to illegal money-making activities.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/enforcement-directorate-searches-prayag-developers-premises-in-nagpur-seizes-1-95-crore-cash/135421268?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-418225/135421268.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Birla Corporation's profit falls 58.6% to \u20b937 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "Birla Corporation Ltd faced a significant 58.58 percent decline in consolidated profits for the September quarter of FY27. However, revenue from operations saw a rise of 9.46 percent, totaling Rs 2,415.42 crore year-on-year. Factors such as depressed cement prices and heavy rains hampered construction in key markets, while soaring input costs for clinker and fuel dented profitability.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/birla-corporations-profit-falls-58-6-to-37-crore-in-q2-fy27/135420885?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-51572/135420885.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}, {"title": "Property registrations in Mumbai  rise 9% to 12,690 units in October 2026: Knight Frank", "para": "In October 2026, Mumbai saw a surge in property registrations, hitting 12,690 units, which reflects a nine percent increase from